    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup is anchored by **Josh Naylor**, who carries our highest efficiency score of 72.69. Facing Springs, **Josh Naylor** benefits from a massive 10% park factor bump and a favorable 4.84 xERA matchup, allowing him to capitalize on the high-contact profile we need. Joining him as a top-tier play is **James Wood** (69.09), whose 0.415 xwOBA and leadoff spot provide a high floor for Runs. While **Vinnie Pasquantino** (70.55) faces a respectable Sonny Gray, his 14% platoon edge against the righty makes him an auto-start. We are also tracking the stolen base potential for **Corbin Carroll** (65.51); despite facing the southpaw Gore, his score is buoyed by a slow opposing pitcher delivery, which elevates his utility in our scarcity-focused build.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Max Muncy** (56.31), who sat just shy of our starting threshold. While **Max Muncy** enjoys a strong 10% park boost against Kirby, the optimizer favored **Austin Riley** (56.83) due to a 65-PA BvP historical edge, which provided the marginal delta required to edge him out of the bench. Meanwhile, **Cole Young** (58.73) remains in the lineup despite a sub-optimal 8th-order spot; he is buoyed by a 19% SP skill advantage against Springs and an elite park factor that forces our hand. We are comfortable benching **Isaac Paredes** (47.09) and **Travis Bazzana** (45.57), as their matchups against high-end arms like Rasmussen and Taj Bradley suppress their efficiency below our daily requirements. \n\nAs we approach first pitch, be aware that **Gabriel Moreno** (55.14) faces a slight drag due to his platoon disadvantage against Gore, though his position in the #3 hole mitigates some of that risk. We are also closely monitoring **Zach McKinstry** (40.25), who is hovering dangerously close to our \"Below Floor\" threshold; if the confirmed lineups shift or weather impacts the Adams start, he is the primary candidate to be pulled to preserve our game caps. Elsewhere on the depth chart, players like **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Griffin Conine**, and **Edwin Arroyo** are relegated to bench duty as we prioritize the superior matchup data driving the starters above.",
